reims-vgpu: the present capture converts the leased readback in place.

Every accepted DisplaySwap on a host whose window is not engine-presented
(the vphone: `window_publish no_window`, `capture_sampling light=0`) reads
the compositor's 1206x2622 RGBA16F front back for the CPU retain
(`frame_bgra`). Before: `read_resident_bgra` copied the 25 MiB staging
buffer into a fresh `Vec` (ReadbackDelivery::Copy), narrowed it through the
half-float LUT into a fresh 12 MiB RGBA8 `Vec`, exchanged R and B across
it, and the drain then walked the retain again for `present_content`'s
`rgb_nz`/`max_rgb`: four whole-frame passes and two allocations under the
device lock, 11-22 ms per present measured on this host (copy 2-9 ms, LUT
5-8 ms, exchange 1.2 ms, walk 0.9 ms; plus the ~1.6 ms fence), which is
`drain_ops op0x08_us / op0x08_n` on a running device (measured:
111-178 ms/s at 6-11 presents/s, 11-22 ms each).
Now: `engine::capture_resident_bgra_into` borrows the staging buffer
(`read_target_texels_consumable`, ReadbackDelivery::Lease) and
`present_capture::convert_with_stats` writes BGRA8 straight into the
recycled capture scratch, in pixel-independent bands on up to four scoped
threads, taking `bgra_rgb_stats`'s figures block by block while the bytes
are in cache; the drain takes those figures (`PresentState::capture_stats`,
cleared at the top of every capture, set only by a resident capture whose
buffer becomes the retain) instead of rescanning. 1.3-1.9 ms for the same
frame on the same host.
Same bytes: `Rgba8Narrowing::convert_to_bgra8` is `convert` followed by the
R/B exchange (same table, same slots; the RGBA16F arm is fused, every other
arm is the two-step form), per-pixel independent, and taking `need` bytes is
the old `truncate(need)`. Same refusals and decline lines
(`present_capture reason=…`, `readback_texel_not_scanout`, the
`target_read_narrowed` route); the prior retain is kept on every refusal.
Nothing the guest reads changes: the retain feeds the console paint and
the window only. New route `present_capture_fused` counts the rail.
Tests: pixel_format::convert_to_bgra8_tests (all 65 536 half words in every
channel slot, every plan, refusals); engine::present_capture::tests (the
vphone geometry banded across threads, every plan at block/band edges, the
leading-pixel truncation, refusals, black frames) against the old
narrow + exchange + bgra_rgb_stats rail; vk_engine_parity::
the_in_place_present_capture_is_the_copying_capture on RADV (a 613x431
RGBA16F resident seeded with NaN/inf/negative/subnormal/tie words and a
BGRA8 surface: identical bytes and figures to read_resident_bgra, twice,
plus truncation and the over-long refusal).

